# Apex manufacturing conventions

This repository sets up a Business Central manufacturing demo company (Apex). Follow these constraints on every change.

## Identity

- AL publisher: `ApexDemo`
- API publisher: `apex`
- API group: `manufacturing`
- Object ID range: `50100..50299` only. Do not use IDs outside this range.

Custom API routes must use publisher `apex` and group `manufacturing` (for example `/api/apex/manufacturing/v1.0/...`).

## APIs

- Prefer standard Business Central APIs (v2.0 and other first-party endpoints) before adding custom APIs.
- Add a custom API only when a standard API cannot create, update, or expose the required manufacturing data.

## Credentials and secrets

- Never hard-code credentials, tokens, tenant IDs used as secrets, client secrets, or connection strings.
- Read environment values from `.env` / config files that are gitignored. Commit only `.env.example` with placeholders.
- Do not print secrets in logs, tests, README, or Cursor rules.
